<title>LEBANON: Lebanon forecasts 25,000 tonnes sugar output.</title>
<headline>Lebanon forecasts 25,000 tonnes sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon will produce some 25,000 tonnes of sugar in 1996, almost the same as last year, the Office of Cereals and Sugar Beet said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I think this year ... will be about the same as 1995. My estimate it that it will be about 25,000 tonnes,&quot; an official of the cereals office, which is part of the Economy Ministry, told Reuters.</p>
<p>According to the cereals office's figures, Lebanon produced 26,296 tonnes of sugar in 1995, much higher than 1994's 20,600 tonnes, mainly due to a rise in sugar levels in sugar beet.</p>
<p>Lebanon imports the rest of its annual sugar requirements of 80,000-90,000 tonnes from Cuba or the European Union.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602056</p>
</text>
